    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, whose elite 80.98 score makes him our premier play against McGreevy. His leadoff status, combined with a favorable 4.53 xERA matchup and strong platoon dynamics, maximizes his potential for both runs and stolen bases. Close behind are **Yordan Alvarez** (66.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (66.79), both of whom benefit from prime lineup positions and high xwOBA metrics. **Junior Caminero** (65.71) and **Lars Nootbaar** (64.61) also project as high-efficiency starts, with **Lars Nootbaar** specifically receiving a significant boost from a strong platoon advantage and a favorable park factor, despite a 4.65 xERA opponent.\n\nWhile the optimizer favored our top starters, the decision to leave **Nelson Velazquez** (43.81) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While he holds a respectable floor, he ultimately fell short of our threshold due to a lack of platoon upside against Hancock compared to the higher-ceiling options like **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Trea Turner** (63.78). We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key players; notably, **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are locked in assuming their standard top-of-order roles, but any deviation in the official lineups could necessitate a recalibration. Meanwhile, **Kazuma Okamoto** remains a start despite a concerning 2.81 xERA matchup against Schlittler, as his base projection allows him to clear our minimum efficiency requirements. Managers should keep a close watch on **Christian Yelich**; although he is currently active, his score of 56.01 is suppressed by a negative platoon shift, keeping him firmly in the \"marginal\" territory for today's contest.",
